<title>FRANCE: EU clears 400,000 tns flour exports - official say.</title>
<headline>EU clears 400,000 tns flour exports - official say.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union cleared bids for the export 400,000 tonnes of flour with licences carrying a daily five Ecus per tonne refund, a European Union official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders bid for the refunds Tuesday, before the EU withdrew the refund, replacing with a nil value.</p>
<p>The official also added the EU would probably accept bids for the export of 70,000 tonnes of soft wheat grain with nil value refunds, when the deadline for accepting these bids expires on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
